\tag{fdip}
\title{What survives repeated blocking}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{A compatible hierarchical family can retain an arbitrary positive
[profile](fdip-01CJ). Finite-range couplings on a periodic grid
give another way to vary the microscopic interaction while observing
averages at a fixed scale. Which data distinguish the limits of these
two kinds of families, and which observations recover those data?}

